text:
jess: Noticing a sharp regression on console dashboard load after this morning's canary. Heatmap + sparklines are stuttering on first paint.
infra-bot: Canary deploy 2026.03.20-canary-14 finished at 08:07 UTC. Promoted to prod at 08:12.
rick: Which pages? Any traces or quick numbers?
jess: /dashboards/org/usage and /dashboards/metrics/heatmap. LCP jumped from ~160ms -> ~720ms on cold loads. Link to trace (internal): https://perf.internal/trace/zz9
amanda: CI artifacts show telemetry-client chunk grew by ~190KB gzipped. Chunk name: telemetry-client~shared.js
ben: That size bump could explain it if telemetry is loaded sync in entry. Can someone paste console entry init lines?
jess: snippet from console/src/entry-client.tsx:

```
import './polyfills';
import { initTelemetry } from '@redwood/telemetry/client';
initTelemetry({ env: 'prod', sampleRate: 0.1 });
hydrateRoot(document.getElementById('root'), <App />);
```

qa: I ran a local 3G/4xCPU emulation and reproduced ~720ms main-thread blocking task around telemetry init.
ben: Looks like initTelemetry now pulls in the full metrics parser + remote config sync synchronously. We recently added a small JSON schema validator and a tiny wasm decoder that triggers sync parsing.
ux: Any UX rollout flags touching prefetch or render hints? Wondering if new prefetch + blocking init amplifies visible jank.
amanda: Prefetch hints were tweaked last week but only affect module preload hints. The visible regression aligns with the telemetry bundle size and a sync parse task in the flamechart.
rick: Proposed short-term mitigations:
- revert canary promotion to previous prod
- lazy-load telemetry in entry and use a minimal event queue stub
- add perf gate in CI for changes that touch telemetry-client
jess: I'll open a tiny revert PR for prod promotion and a follow-up patch to lazy import. Patch sketch:

```
// entry-client.tsx
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
  // defer heavy telemetry init off main hydration path
  import('@redwood/telemetry/client').then(m => m.initTelemetry({ env: 'prod', sampleRate: 0.1 }));
} else {
  // keep sync init for dev to preserve local debugging ergonomics
  initTelemetry({ env: 'dev', sampleRate: 1 });
}
hydrateRoot(...)
```
deploy-bot: Rollback request for service "console-frontend" by jess submitted.
infra-bot: Rollback executed 
 at 08:25 UTC 
 -> service reverted to 2026.03.19-prod-82.
qa: After rollback quick-check on prod: cold LCP back to ~170ms. Heatmaps render normally.
ben: Follow-ups created: RW-5401 (defer telemetry init + queue stub), RW-5402 (split telemetry-client chunks), RW-5403 (add CI perf gate + emulation tests).
amanda: We'll also audit any other libs that may pull in sync parsing (wasm/text-decoder) and add a checklist before changing entry imports.
jess: Thx folks. I'll push the lazy-import PR and include CI perf run. Marking this thread resolved for now. :white_check_mark:
